[907.462938, "o", "[approval] bash: bash -c 'source ~/.bashrc; klee --help | head -n 20' — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash bash -c 'source ~/.bashrc; klee --help | head -n 20'\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  glimmer-30b — 103 tool call(s) so far\r\nInstallation complete.\r\n\r\n* STP 2.4.1 built from source with `--auto-download` and installed to `/usr/local`\r\n* KLEE 3.4-pre built in `/tmp/klee-build` with:\r\n  * `LLVM_DIR=/usr/lib/llvm-16/lib/cmake/llvm`\r\n  * `ENABLE_SOLVER_STP=ON`, `STP_DIR=/usr/local`\r\n  * `LLVMCC=/usr/bin/clang-16`, `LLVMCXX=/usr/bin/clang++-16`\r\n  * `ENABLE_TCMALLOC=OFF`, `ENABLE_UNIT_TESTS=OFF`, `ENABLE_SYSTEM_TESTS=OFF`\r\n  * POSIX runtime disabled → no uClibc\r\n  * STPSolver.cpp patched to drop the removed `vc_useRiss`/`vc_isUsingRiss` symbols from STP 2.4\r\n\r\nEnvironment made persistent in `~/.bashrc`:\r\n```\r\nexport PATH=$PATH:/tmp/klee-build/bin\r\nexport CPATH=$CPATH:/tmp/klee-source/include\r\n```\r\n\r\nVerification after sourcing:\r\n```\r\n$ source ~/.bashrc\r\n$ which klee\r\n/tmp/klee-build/bin/klee\r\n$ klee --version\r\nKLEE 3.4-pre (https://klee-se.org/)\r\n  Build mode: Release (Asserts: ON)\r\n  ...\r\nUbuntu LLVM version 16.0.6\r\n$ echo $CPATH\r\n:/tmp/klee-source/include\r\n$ find $CPATH -name klee.h\r\n/tmp/klee-source/include/klee/klee.h\r\n```\r\n\r\n`klee` is now on the command line and the KLEE headers are reachable via `CPATH`.\r\n\r\n[result] role=implementor model=glimmer-30b tools=103 surface=c77f3a48d7b9\r\n"]
